    "bounding box" : [ 97.965, 695.948, 529.965, 736.044 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "A subrepresentation of a representation V of the magnetic point group (G,ϕ) is a subspace W ⊂ V such that the restriction of the G-action to W is also a representation of (G,ϕ). A representation V of (G,ϕ) is irreducible if its only representations are V and 0."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 109.921, 683.652, 446.914, 696.797 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Now, the category of representations of finite magnetic groups is semisimple."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 97.965, 650.214, 529.967, 676.583 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proposition 1.9. Every representation of a finite magnetic group is a sum of irreducible representations."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 97.965, 555.138, 529.97, 642.632 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Which follows from Maschke’s lemma applied to representations of magnetic groups. Lemma 1.10 (Maschke). If W is a subrepresentation of V of a finite magnetic group, then there exists a subrepresentation W′ of V such that V = W ⊕ W′. Proof. Write V as a direct sum V = W ⊕U (with U not necessary a subrepresentation) and consider the projection π1 : V −→ W given by π1(w + u) = w. Define"
